    "description": "Product engineer at an aluminum casting foundry tasked to design processes for new parts through various operations such as wax, shell, foundry, and heat treat. Products must meet stringent requirements of aerospace or other applicable material specifications.\n\nWorked in the foundry to gather data, audit process, and create improvement plans to minimize defects.\n\nManaged the heat treat process and tasked to ensure that the operation met NADCAP specifications. Ovens must conform to class 2 oven tolerances, strict calibration schedules, and other related requirements.\n\nConverted legacy quality system to new, windows based ERP system. Migrated part quality requirements, set up the structure of the software to reflect current process, and trained personnel to use the program.",
